    "scientific_audit_and_corrections": {
      "correction_1_static_threshold_fallacy": "Step 17 evaluated Arm 2B at static tau=0.50, reporting FPR=50.55% and claiming unviability. Class-weighting by pos_weight=8.40 mathematically shifts Bayes-optimal logits by ln(8.40) \u2248 +2.13. When evaluated at matched FPR ceilings (10%, 15%, 20%), Arm 2B achieves FNR=60.33%, 51.08%, 43.56%, which is virtually identical to Arm 2A (61.62%, 51.51%, 44.25%) and within ~1.7% of Baseline R (59.90%, 49.35%, 43.30%). Static tau=0.50 comparison measures calibration shift, NOT discriminative failure.",
      "correction_2_two_update_micro_resumption_fallacy": "Step 17 proposed GPU micro-resumption for 2 updates (0.055% of budget) to rescue Arm 2B. Arm 2B peaked at Epoch 1 (600 updates, Val AP 0.3164) and degraded monotonically across 5 epochs (0.3090 -> 0.3089 -> 0.3070 -> 0.3051 -> 0.3080). Adding 2 updates to an overfitted model in Epoch 6 would produce zero measurable change in detector performance. Micro-resumption is scientifically unwarranted.",
      "correction_3_early_stopping_convergence_shift": "Both loss treatment arms experienced earlier validation peaks and earlier degradation than Baseline R: Arm 2B peaked at Epoch 1 (600 up), Arm 2A peaked at Epoch 2 (1,200 up), while Baseline R peaked at Epoch 6 (3,600 up). Loss re-weighting accelerates training fit but increases validation overfitting on Fold 1.",
      "correction_4_unsupported_winner_classification": "Step 17 declared Arm 2A the 'Authoritative Winner'. In reality, at the primary 3,600-update milestone, Arm 2A underperforms Baseline R by Delta AP = -0.008908, fails the registered elevation target (> +0.020), and its acoustic reliance gap degraded to +0.009869 (falling below the +0.010 registered threshold). Even at its secondary peak, Arm 2A is only +0.000189 above Baseline R. Arm 2A is an unproven exploratory candidate, NOT a proven winner."
